## Git Workflow (Summary)

**Branching:** Feature branches (`feature/<description>`)
**Commits:** Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, etc.) **with user story reference**
**Pre-commit Hooks:** ✅ Configured (lint, format, type-check, tests, build)
**Merge Strategy:** [Squash and merge / Merge commits / Rebase]

**REQUIRED:** All commits implementing user stories MUST include:
```
Implements: docs/features/us-XXX-<story-name>.md
```

**Example:**
```bash
git commit -m "feat: add [feature name]

- [Implementation detail]
- [Implementation detail]
- Tests: [X]% coverage

Implements: docs/features/us-XXX-<story-name>.md

 

```

**Why This Matters:**
- Provides traceability between code and requirements
- Required for updating `docs/high-level-user-stories.md`
- Helps code reviewers check against acceptance criteria

See `docs/git-workflow.md` for complete workflow and conventions.

